Spec: Change Boundary Guide

Purpose:
  Document feature-scoped Change Boundary semantics, lifecycle-specific target discovery, regeneration, unresolved handling, staleness, and disposable derived-state behavior.

Owns:
  ./change-boundary.md

References:
  ../README.sdd
  ./development.sdd
  ../integration/specdd/commands/context.sdd
  ../integration/specdd/commands/validate.sdd
  ../integration/specdd/commands/authorize.sdd
  ../integration/specdd/commands/verify.sdd
  ../integration/specdd/scripts/workflow_gate.sdd

Must:
  The guide explains how target discovery becomes more precise from planning through task generation.
  The guide explains deterministic regeneration from canonical Spec Kit artifacts and fresh SpecDD resolver output without copying persistent SpecDD constraints.
  The guide distinguishes advisory unresolved planning context from unresolved implementation authority that cannot grant permission.
  The guide explains when a Change Boundary is refreshed and when the existing boundary must remain unchanged as the operation authority snapshot.
  The guide explains stale-boundary conditions and the required refresh points.
  The guide presents `boundary.json` as disposable derived state that can be deleted and rebuilt from canonical sources.
  Installation and development-host maintenance remain delegated to the README and development guide rather than duplicated here.

Done when:
  A maintainer can determine when a Change Boundary is created, refreshed, preserved as a snapshot, rejected as stale, and safely regenerated.
